  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/89df4e37-4e9b-4c51-a5c8-9e7f77d7b38a.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 221px;\"/></p><p>In steady state:</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math></p><p>Current through the branches with resistance, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Now, potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>and potential drop <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Charge on the first capacitor, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo> </mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Charge on the second capacitor, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
